 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to establishing\nmicrochipping standards, registration of microchips and the examination of\nseized animals; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the\nagriculture and markets law relating to establishing microchipping standards;\nrelating to the registration of microchips; and relating to the examination of\nseized animals and animals taken possession of, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 4570-A and A. 1839-B, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof; and to repeal certain provisions of the agriculture and markets law\nrelating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S7317",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7317-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §111-b, amd §111-a, Ag & Mkts L; amd §3, Chap of 2017 (as proposed in S. 4570-A and A. 1839-B)",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7317\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to estab-\nlishing microchipping standards, registration of microchips and the\nexamination of seized animals; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2017, amending the agriculture and markets law relating to establishing\nmicrochipping standards; relating to the registration of microchips; and\nrelating to the examination of seized animals and animals taken\npossession of, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 4570-A and A.\n1839-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and to repeal certain\nprovisions of the agriculture and markets law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would provide for a standardization of technology used in\nmicrochips implanted into companion animals; require the examination of\nrescued companion animals; and require such facilities to notify owners\nif they are in possession of an animal they believe to be missing.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis chapter amendment adds language to section 111-a, which would allow\nthe commissioner to promulgate rules to have veterinarians, animal shel-\nters and other similar entities to have a microchip reader capable of\nreading any commercially available microchip implanted in a cat or dog.\nThis amendment also removes mandatory language that originally required\nthat the rules and regulations be provided for collecting, sharing, and\ndissemination of chip identification. This chapter amendment requires\nthe appointment of an advisory committee.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMicrochipping is an effective means to reunite lost pets found by animal\ncontrol officers or brought to animal shelters or other entities with\ntheir caregivers. This bill requires the Commissioner of Agriculture and\nMarkets to create and implement rules and regulations to standardize\nmicrochip technology. This bill also requires compliance with the rules\nthat govern the registration of microchips and the information gathered.\nThis bill also requires animal organizations to examine the animal with-\nin twenty-four hours for identifying marks, and if suspected lost or\nstolen, should make a reasonable effort to contact the owner.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone Noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nAs amended, this act would take effect immediately.\n",
